    {
      "id": "gqav8dq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ENVIRONMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Environment consists of biotic and abiotic components interacting with living organisms.",
        "Natural resources are categorized into Renewable (inexhaustible) and Non-Renewable (exhaustible) resources.",
        "Forest, Water, and Soil resources form the essential pillars of terrestrial ecosystem stability.",
        "Conservation of biodiversity and natural resources is imperative to control pollution and global warming."
      ],
      "id": "vw39esz"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter",
